waitpid - collect exit, stop or continue status for a child

SYNOPSIS
    int waitpid(int pid, int *status, int options);

DESCRIPTION
    A positive PID selects a child, 0 the caller's process group, -1
    any child, and a value below -1 a group by its absolute ID.
    WNOHANG makes the wait nonblocking. WUNTRACED reports stops and
    WCONTINUED reports resumption. Interpret status using <wait.h>.
    Return the child PID, 0 for no event with WNOHANG, or -1 on error.

SEE ALSO
    kill(1)
